nvidia: coarse runtime D3cold (NVreg_DynamicPowerManagement=1): power the GPU off while no client has it open

The port stubbed RM's runtime power hooks (nv_dynamic_power_available() false, nv_indicate_idle/not_idle
NOT_SUPPORTED), so an attached GPU idles in D0 forever. On the ThinkPad X1 Extreme Gen 5 that is the RTX 3080 Ti
heating the machine to an EC power cut (53 -> 94 C in ten minutes, scripts/patches/0005).

RM already decides when (src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c). In COARSE mode its refcount drops to
zero after attach and after the last close, once RM has shut the adapter down, and it calls nv_indicate_idle().
The first open calls nv_indicate_not_idle() before rm_init_adapter() and needs the GPU powered when that returns.
Linux implements the pair with the PCI core's runtime PM: D3hot, then the root port's ACPI _PR3 power resource off.
nvidia_rtd3.c is that executor for illumos:

- attach: the parent's _PR3 names a PowerResource and NVreg_DynamicPowerManagement is exactly 1. Then
  rm_init_dynamic_power_management() is told _PR3 is present (it was told NV_FALSE), and
  nv_dynamic_power_available() is true. Any other value (the default 3, or 2 = FINE, which needs the GC6 _DSM
  handshake and runtime suspend callbacks) changes nothing.
- attach also offlines the GPU's other functions (HDMI audio), which lose power with it, before any of them
  attaches, as tzmon does at boot; offline nodes are never attached again. If one will not go offline, RTD3 stays
  off for this GPU. They stay offline until the next boot.
- idle: a taskq waits 10 s of uninterrupted idle. It then takes ldata_lock without sleeping on it (so a detach
  that holds it can always drain the taskq) and re-checks that no client and no RM state exist. It saves config
  space, puts the GPU in D3hot and evaluates _PR3 _OFF: the same sequence tzmon runs at boot.
- not idle: waits for a running off to finish and evaluates _ON. As Linux's pcie_wait_for_link does, it sends no
  config request to the GPU until the root port reports Data Link Layer Link Active (the X1E's port supports that
  report), then waits 100 ms. It then waits up to 5 s for the GPU to answer config reads, restores config space
  and goes to D0. A GPU that does not come back fails the open (NV_ERR_GPU_IS_LOST).
- detach powers the GPU on first, since RM teardown reads BAR0. quiesce, DDI_SUSPEND and DDI_RESUME skip config
  access while it is off, and DDI_RESUME evaluates _OFF again in case the firmware powered the slot back up.
- kstat nvidia:<inst>:rtd3 {off, offs, ons}.
